              "help": {
                "text": "1. **Use `ProcessBuilder(List.of(...))`** with the executable + each argument as a separate list element: `new ProcessBuilder(\"git\", \"log\", \"--max-count=10\", \"--\", userPath).start()`. The list-form does not invoke a shell, so injection metacharacters (`;`, `|`, `` ` ``, `$()`) are inert.\n2. **Never use `Runtime.getRuntime().exec(String)`** with a string concatenated from user input. The single-string form goes through a `StringTokenizer` and is fragile in addition to being injectable.\n3. **Allowlist user values.** Validate against a fixed regex or `EnumSet`: `if (!ALLOWED_HOSTS.contains(host)) throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"unknown host\");`.\n4. **Use stdlib equivalents instead of shelling out.** `java.nio.file.Files.copy/move/delete` not `cp/mv/rm`, the JGit library not `git`, Apache Commons Compress not `tar`/`zip`. Shellouts are rarely the right tool inside a JVM.\n5. **Use `Process.waitFor(timeout, TimeUnit.SECONDS)` and `Process.destroyForcibly()`** to bound runaway children. Capture both stdout and stderr to avoid back-pressure deadlocks.\n6. **Run the JVM under a SecurityManager / SELinux profile / Docker user namespace** so even successful command injection has limited blast radius.\n\nPriority: IMMEDIATE"
