            {
              "id": "shell_injection",
              "name": "shell_injection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "shell_injection"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Command injection vulnerabilities in shell scripts occur when user-controlled data is incorporated into system commands without proper validation or sanitization. Shell scripts are particularly vulnerable due to their direct interaction with the operating system and the powerful command substitution and expansion features. Attackers can exploit these to execute arbitrary commands on the host operating system."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "**Prevention Strategies:**\n1. **Quote variables**: Always quote variables with double quotes\n2. **Input validation**: Validate input against strict patterns\n3. **Avoid eval**: Never use eval with user-controlled data\n4. **Use arrays**: Use bash arrays for safer argument handling\n5. **Whitelist approach**: Only allow known, safe values\n\n**Secure Implementation:**\n```bash\n# Secure: Quoted variables\nls \"$user_input\"\n\n# Secure: Input validation\nif [[ \"$filename\" =~ ^[a-zA-Z0-9._-]+$ ]]; then\n    cat \"$filename\"\nfi\n\n# Secure: Array usage\ncommand_args=(\"ls\" \"-la\" \"$user_directory\")\n\"${command_args[@]}\"\n```"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-78",
                  "OWASP/A03:2021"
                ],
                "precision": "medium",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "cwe": "CWE-78",
                "owasp": "A03:2021 - Injection"
              }
            },
