            {
              "id": "dependabot_missing_cooldown",
              "name": "Dependabot Missing Cooldown",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Dependabot Missing Cooldown"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "[Semgrep · package_managers.dependabot.dependabot-missing-cooldown.dependabot-missing-cooldown · CWE-829 · A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures]\n\nThis Dependabot configuration does not set a cooldown period. Newly published packages can be malicious or unstable. Add a `cooldown` block with `default-days: 7` to each `package-ecosystem` entry under `updates` to wait 7 days before proposing updates to newly published package versions. Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/dependabot/dependabot-version-updates/configuration-options-for-the-dependabot.yml-file#cooldown"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the guidance in the referenced rule docs: https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/dependabot/dependabot-version-updates/configuration-options-for-the-dependabot.yml-file#cooldown; https://semgrep.dev/r/package_managers.dependabot.dependabot-missing-cooldown.dependabot-missing-cooldown\n\nReferences & resources:\n  - https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/dependabot/dependabot-version-updates/configuration-options-for-the-dependabot.yml-file#cooldown\n  - https://semgrep.dev/r/package_managers.dependabot.dependabot-missing-cooldown.dependabot-missing-cooldown"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-829",
                  "OWASP/A08:2021"
                ],
                "precision": "medium",
                "security-severity": "5",
                "cwe": "CWE-829",
                "owasp": "A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "github_actions_mutable_action_tag",
              "name": "Github Actions Mutable Action Tag",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Github Actions Mutable Action Tag"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "[Semgrep · yaml.github-actions.security.github-actions-mutable-action-tag.github-actions-mutable-action-tag · CWE-1357 · A08:2021 - Software and Data Integrity Failures]\n\nGitHub Actions step uses a mutable tag or branch reference. Tags and branch names can be silently repointed by the action owner, enabling supply-chain attacks — as seen in the trivy-action and kics-github-action compromises. Pin the reference to a full 40-character commit SHA instead, e.g. `uses: actions/checkout@8ade135a41bc03ea155e62e844d188df1ea18608`.\n\nRelated CWEs: CWE-1357, CWE-353"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Follow the guidance in the referenced rule docs: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/security-guides/security-hardening-for-github-actions#using-third-party-actions; https://semgrep.dev/r/yaml.github-actions.security.github-actions-mutable-action-tag.github-actions-mutable-action-tag\n\nReferences & resources:\n  - https://docs.github.com/en/actions/security-guides/security-hardening-for-github-actions#using-third-party-actions\n  - https://semgrep.dev/r/yaml.github-actions.security.github-actions-mutable-action-tag.github-actions-mutable-action-tag"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-1357"
                ],
                "precision": "medium",
                "security-severity": "5",
                "cwe": "CWE-1357"
              }
            },
            {
