          "ruleId": "deserialization",
          "ruleIndex": 9,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Java deserialization vulnerabilities arise when applications deserialize untrusted data using ObjectInputStream.readObject() or similar methods. Since Java serialization can reconstruct entire object graphs including executable code, attackers can craft malicious serialized objects that execute arbitrary code during deserialization. This is particularly dangerous because it can lead to remote code execution without any user interaction."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
